// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ArachnosData 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3668858298" "Arachnos Data"
// DetailString :
"P2523402815" "You retrieved a large amount of data that Arachnos had gathered over time from Praetoria. Looking it over, one part seems concerning, especially given your status as an Incarnate. Recluse believes that Emperor Cole may have a closer connection to the Well of the Furies more than anyone. There is a comment by Recluse himself, wondering if this means that Cole can somehow influence the Well with his own willpower."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PortalNormal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2519706678" "War Work Data Core"
// DetailString :
"P4239594658" "You retrieved this data core from one of the War Works within Portal Corp. You're able to use Vanguard technology to hack into it and gather data regarding Cole's invasion plans. One thing stands out to you: whoever programmed these machines made sure that they would not target a civilian under any circumstances. You're unable to tell if this was done by the programmer or an order directly from Tyrant."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - GrandvilleAmbushed 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P876094588" "Recluse's Gambit"
// DetailString :
"P3621688800" "You were forced to fight off a squad of Lord Recluse's kill team within Grandville tower, despite the fact that you were sent in to help alleviate the situation. It seems Recluse is willing to make a strike against anyone he deems as a threat, even in the most dire circumstances."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - GrandvilleNormal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3985540214" "Grandville Normal"
// DetailString :
"P3293143404" "You were able to fend off the incoming ambushes of War Works within Grandville tower, ensuring that the Praetorians did not gain a foothold within Grandville. It may be difficult to believe that saving the tower can be a <i>good</i> thing, but the alternative would be allowing the Praetorians to have all of Grandville as a secured base of operations."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL9_RWZ_TinMage_SouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P1847139557" "Goliath Memory Core"
// tDetailString :
"P111669055" "You took a memory core from a Goliath War Walker during your fight against them in Neutropolis. There's a lot of information that you can use from the core, either for the good of Primal Earth or for your own ends. It reminds you of an experience you call...<br><br><b>The Praetorian Offensive</b><br><br>It all began when you formed a team to push back the invading Praetorians with a robot named Tin Mage Mark II.  You travelled to Nerva Archipelago to retake Crimson Cove from the Praetorians. It was there that you discovered a secret base where War Walkers were being manufactured. You destroyed the base and also defeated Director 11, one of the enigmatic members of Malta's council of Directors.<br><br>Tin Mage then requested your team to guard a conference between members of Longbow and members of Arachnos. As expected, the War Works attacked the conference, but you were able to push them back and secure Portal Corp, and just in time. Tin Mage alerted you to the fact that the Praetorians were planning to launch their full army through a portal in Neutropolis.<br><br>You went through the portal in Portal Corp and attacked the heart of Neutropolis, defeating Neuron, Bobcat, and their initial force of Goliaths, putting a halt to the Praetorians' initial invasion plans. The war may not be over, but now Cole knows there are forces in Primal Earth that he can't easily swat down."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3513648125" "Greetings. My name is Tin Mage Mark II, the latest model of Tin Mage, rebuilt by Vanguard after my unfortunate and assumed demise at the hands of the Rikti. I have been put in charge of forming yet another assault on an alternate dimension. Perhaps it's due to my experience in attacking other dimensions. Or, rather, the experience of my former make.<br><br>Regardless, the assistance of you and your team is needed on this day. Before we can take the fight to Praetoria, we need to form a united front here in Primal Earth. This means <i>Arachnos</i>. Currently, they are having a dire situation with the Praetorian invasion within Nerva Archipelago. These islands have been disputed for quite some time.<br><br>Vanguard would like to enlist your aid in taking back Nerva from the Praetorians and moving forward to strike a blow against them on their home turf."
// AcceptString :
"P525090842" "My team is ready."
// SendOffString :
"P1400547159" "Excellent, we're going to run this operation as efficiently as possible.<br><br>There is a Vanguard helicopter waiting to bring you into Nerva Archipelago. <color orange>Once there, you will need to clear out the 'War Walkers' from the topside, then uncover the Praetorian base of operations in Nerva.</color> We believe the Praetorians have established a secret base within Nerva, as there was no indication that they 'teleported' in. Rather, it appears they activated a hidden base and overwhelmed the area.<br><br>Oh, and you may wish to be careful. Malta has been making routine assaults against the Praetorians in Nerva. I believe they are trying to retrieve the Praetorian technology for their own use."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2882323532" "Retake Crimson Cove"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4058669300" "It is curious that Malta has chosen this moment to make their strike. Perhaps we will find out why."
// TaskTitle :
"P2119030436" "<color deepskyblue>The Praetorian Offensive</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P4236671879" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: Bid for Power</color>"

